from pathlib import Path
import re,json
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
caps={
'method_modules':r'''Exact reversible representation and preparation-inclusive token accounting. (a) A three-vertex, two-edge excerpt of confirmation graph 87 before and after recoding; the complete graph has 28 nodes and 112 edge entries. The inverse dictionary restores original identifiers; positions are display geometry. (b) Inner-ring angles split complete mean cost into source and reader usage; outer-ring angles split input and output. Angles alone encode fractions. The total is 5,344.46 tokens per prefix answer, averaged over 24 sources and 48 readers; labels are rounded. Every answer pays full preparation. (c) Native reader input for graph 87's first seed, not population means. Dictionary storage and CPU preprocessing are separate; output caps do not imply matched realized compute.''',
'paired_models_20261006':r'''Qwen3 packages on the same twelve questions, five reader seeds per graph, from two separately audited 240-call studies. (a,b) All graph means: circles denote parents, squares BFS. Perpendicular offsets separate observations. Shaded curves are descriptive densities (F1 reflected at both bounds, bandwidth 0.08; tokens reflected at zero, bandwidth 2,000), with common height scales within metrics. Ceiling conditions retain all twelve observations without smoothing. F1/EM means are printed; the dashed reference is always-empty F1. Costs charge all five sources and one reader. (c) Existing descriptive stratified graph-bootstrap intervals; dashed lines denote zero. The 4B zero-width placement interval reflects the observed ceiling, not population equivalence. Packages generate their own traces; this is not a size-only comparison. Eighteen length-terminated 4B direct readings retain zero scores.''',
'user_benefit':r'''Discovery study, separate from confirmation. Each block retains twelve graph means, with two reader repeats averaged within graphs; circles denote parents and squares BFS. Descriptive boundary-reflected F1 densities use bandwidth 0.08 and equal peak height; all observations remain visible. Printed values give F1/EM means. Below, arrows connect original, compact and prefix arm means in that order; circles, squares and diamonds identify these arms. Score and complete-token scales are shared across blocks. Costs charge full preparation. Capacity packages have different serving allowances; complete original inputs would not fit the nonexecuted 8K reference. Input fit did not meet the predefined nonempty exact-in-both-repeats practical criterion. Short-block results are exploratory.''',
'official_graph_confirmatory_20261006':r'''Prospective twelve-graph replication from independently rescored responses. (a) Curves track the same graph across direct, front-trace and back-trace conditions, separately for BFS and parent queries. Colours and identifiers distinguish graphs; smooth connections interpolate only between discrete conditions. F1 averages five reader seeds. Horizontal marker offsets separate coincident scores without changing F1. (b) All twelve complete-token graph means per arm with descriptive zero-reflected densities, bandwidth 2,000 and equal peak height; printed values are means. Trace answers pay all five sources and one reader, direct answers only the reader. All 240 calls completed; format and termination failures retain prescribed zero scores. Both empty-gold graph units remain in all analyses. Paired contrasts and existing descriptive intervals are reported in the text and tables.''',
'output_budget_20261006':r'''Sequential output-cap diagnostic on the same twelve Qwen3-4B questions. (a) Each colour tracks one identified graph under direct-output caps of 8,192 and 28,672, with five seeds averaged. Curves interpolate between discrete conditions only; horizontal marker offsets expose overlapping ceiling observations without changing F1. Old length-terminated responses retain zero scores. (b) All twelve complete-token graph means per condition and descriptive zero-reflected densities (bandwidth 2,000, equal peak height); printed totals are means. Trace costs include all five sources. New direct answers and both trace placements reach the observed F1/EM ceiling. This known-question diagnostic matches maximum generated allowances, not total compute, and establishes neither population equivalence nor isolated causality.''',
'source_qualification_figure':r'''Native source qualification on eight official graphs and two repeats, excluding calibration. (a) Every saved call is located by its input and generated tokens. Circles and triangles distinguish seeds; connectors join repeats of the same identified graph, not a fitted relationship. Teal denotes F1 equal to one and orange lower F1. Thin leader lines connect identifiers to pair midpoints. (b) Fourteen readings have F1 and EM equal to one; graph 504 has F1 0 and 0.857 and EM 0 for both seeds. All points have fixed size; no inferential error bars are shown. No trace reuse was tested.''',
'interrupted_study_figure':r'''Context and execution boundaries of the native five-trace trial. (a) Annular angles partition all 480 formal slots, excluding calibration, into qualified responses, budget declines, unqualified responses and unreached slots; counts are printed. Unreached slots are not failed answers. (b) Measured first-graph inputs against the input limit after output reservation (98,240) and configured context (131,072), shown by dashed thresholds. (c) Open endpoints delimit F1 identification bounds over all sixteen planned graph outcomes; numeric labels give both endpoints. These are not confidence intervals. Missing outcomes prevent a quality conclusion.''',
'partial_state_display':r'''Early-state adaptation after interrupted execution. Annular angles show known versus unknown outcomes for each arm, with all 32 planned outputs retained in the denominator. Open endpoints delimit F1 identification bounds and printed pairs give both endpoints; these are not sampling intervals. Cost labels marked $\geq$ give known charged deployment tokens divided by 32 planned predictions; every total is incomplete. Each state prediction pays full source cost. Unknown outcomes are not assigned failure scores. The ranges do not establish a quality gain or efficiency advantage.''',
'interrupted_indexed_figure':r'''Interrupted representation comparison by thinking mode. Coverage rings show known versus unknown readings out of sixteen per arm. Teal F1 and orange EM endpoint pairs give identification bounds over all planned slots; the F1 bounds are also printed. Zero-width ranges represent complete observed arms, not absence of sampling uncertainty. Costs are observed input-plus-output token sums, with $\geq$ marking incomplete lower bounds. CPU preprocessing (1.188\,s) and compact-dictionary storage (36,612 bytes) remain separate. Unknown readings were not resent.''',
'official_graph_identity_recode':r'''Identity recoding on eight graph units and two seeds per arm. (a) Each colour tracks one identified graph across original, compact and long-alias representations, separately by task. F1 averages the two seeds; curved links interpolate between discrete conditions only. Horizontal marker offsets separate coincident scores without changing F1. (b) Fixed-radius annuli encode input/output token shares by angle, not total cost by size; centres print observed totals charging both readings per graph. Mean F1 and existing descriptive 95\% intervals appear below. Dictionary storage and CPU preprocessing are separate. All graph information survives reversible recoding; a positive estimate does not override the failed follow-up gate.''',
'official_graph_reasoning_mode':r'''Thinking-mode and fixed-route comparison on sixteen graph units and two paired seeds. (a) Four task--length strata with four graphs each; arrows connect thinking-off circles to thinking-on diamonds in the quality--cost plane. Axes are shared, F1 averages graphs, and token totals sum seed-averaged costs within strata. Arrows do not imply a continuous response curve or causal isolation. (b) All-graph complete-token totals, F1 means and existing descriptive 95\% intervals. Route reuses the prespecified parents/off and BFS/on subsets of saved calls. Lower cost accompanies lower observed quality; no trace-order mechanism is tested.'''
}
changes=[]
for name in ['main.tex','migration_primary_body.tex','early_state_detail.tex']:
 p=P/name;s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
 def change(m):
  block=m.group();key=next((k for k in caps if '/'+k+'/publication.pdf' in block),None)
  if not key:return block
  if key=='method_modules':path='figures/visual_pilot_20261015/method/design.pdf'
  elif key=='paired_models_20261006':path='figures/visual_pilot_20261015/models/design.pdf'
  else:path=f'figures/refined_r_20261015/{key}/publication.pdf'
  block=block.replace(f'figures/distinctive_r_20261015/{key}/publication.pdf',path)
  pos=block.index(r'\caption{')+len(r'\caption{');depth=1;i=pos
  while depth:
   if block[i]=='{' and block[i-1]!='\\':depth+=1
   elif block[i]=='}' and block[i-1]!='\\':depth-=1
   i+=1
  block=block[:pos]+caps[key]+block[i-1:];changes.append(key);return block
 s=re.sub(r'\\begin\{figure\}.*?\\end\{figure\}',change,s,flags=re.S);p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
assert len(changes)==11,changes
(P/'revision_evidence_20261015_refined/CAPTIONS.json').write_text(json.dumps(caps,indent=2))
print('Adopted',len(changes),'figures; scientific body unchanged')
